@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

This package provides an Emacs integration to the @uref{https://github.com/jmerle/competitive-companion, Competitive Companion browser extension}. It also provides some commands to speed up the coding-compiling-test loop during online contests.

The package is designed to be minimalistic and as non-intrusive as possible@comma{} while still providing some level of convenience. The idea is that during an online contest@comma{} you turn on the global minor mode. Then@comma{} when you read a problem with the browser extension@comma{} Emacs will automatically download the test cases into a hidden directory next to the implementation file@comma{} without cluttering your folder listing@comma{} and generate an implementation file using your preferred language and template in the contest's folder. When you are done implementing the code and compiling it@comma{} the package provides an interactive command that runs the program against the downloaded test cases. Then@comma{} if all outputs matched@comma{} it just lets you know in the minibuffer. Otherwise@comma{} an special buffer pops up with only the failed test cases.

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

This package is currently only available through the GitHub repository. Check installation instructions @uref{https://github.com/luishgh/competitive-companion.el?tab=readme-ov-file#installation, there}.

